# Copy to .env.local. With neither value set, the app runs in demo mode against a
# synthetic catalog and every feature works — see README.

# From https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard. There is no client secret: the app
# uses Authorization Code with PKCE, which does not need one.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Any random string of 32+ characters. Encrypts the session cookie holding your
# Spotify tokens. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# Where Spotify sends people back. Leave this unset and the app uses the origin the
# request arrived on: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback in development, your
# deployed origin in production. Set it only when the two differ — a custom domain
# in front of the deployment, say.
#
# Either way, the value the app ends up using must be registered character for
# character as a redirect URI on the Spotify app, at
# https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard. For a deployment at https://your-host,
# the line to paste there is:
#
#   https://your-host/api/auth/callback
#
# SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=
